    "pages":{
        "home": {
            "default": "Home",
            "description": "Hello! I am Federico Mattucci, a computer science student at the University of Pisa. With this website, I would like to tell you a little bit about myself."
        },
        "experience": {
            "default": "Work Experiences",
            "description": "This section is dedicated to my work and internship experiences."
        },
        "portfolio": {
            "default": "Portfolio",
            "description": "Here you can find some of my projects and works.",
            "photographyDescription": "I became passionate about photography in a completely unexpected way. One day, my father asked me to take some photos of watches he wanted to sell. At the time, I had a phone that didn't have a very good camera and I knew nothing about photography. When I started taking photos, I realised that all the images were full of reflections, overexposed or underexposed. Not having the tools to take good photos, I started to figure out how to “create” them. I made “panels” to use as softboxes using four sheets of paper on which I had printed black pages. These allowed me to remove the reflections, but they also made the photos underexposed. I then created a light with a diffuser, again using white sheets of paper and a spring-loaded arm, in order to better illuminate the watches. Initially, I didn't like it because it was too complicated, but then, as time went by and I took more photos of these objects, I began to develop a passion for it, and that's how I began to study photography."

        },
